<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>

  <!-- ====================================================================
       ALPHA MECHS: THEIRS, NOT OURS

       Alpha Mechs is loaded so the Glitterites can field AM_Daggersnout,
       AM_Phalanx, AM_Goliath and the rest as part of their combined-arms
       raids. The player is not supposed to get any of it: no mechtech
       research, no gestation, no mechanitor gear, no buying it off traders.

       WHAT IS AND IS NOT TOUCHED

       Untouched: every mech PawnKindDef and ThingDef, their bodies,
       abilities, damage defs and sounds. That is the whole reason the mod
       is here, and Archinity.Glitterites references those kinds by name.

       Removed or neutered: only the things the PLAYER interacts with.
       Alpha Mechs keeps its player-facing content in a Biotech submodule
       (1.6/Mods/Biotech, loaded via loadFolders because Biotech is active),
       which is what makes this surgical:

         26 MechGestator RecipeDefs   gestation of every AM mech
         11 mechanitor buildings      band nodes, boosters, rechargers
          8 apparel items             packs, commander suits, prestige gear
          9 ResearchProjectDefs       AM_*Mechtech and the Ultra four

       ORDER MATTERS. The research projects are removed LAST, and the
       referencing defs are neutered rather than deleted, for one specific
       reason: when RimWorld cannot resolve a cross-reference it logs an
       error and OMITS the entry rather than storing null. So deleting the
       research first would strip researchPrerequisites off the buildings
       and leave them buildable with no research at all, which is the exact
       opposite of the intent. Neutering first, deleting second, is safe in
       either resolution order.

       Removing the research also pulls 4,100 Industrial and 3,000 Ultra
       points out of TechBlock's tier totals, which slightly lowers the
       TB_SpacerTechLock and TB_ArchoTechLock costs. That is a side effect,
       not the goal, and it is in the helpful direction.

       Note: xpath predicates use starts-with() on "AM_" so this keeps
       working if Alpha Mechs adds more mechs later.
       ==================================================================== -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Alpha Mechs</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <!-- 1. No gestation.

             Matching on researchPrerequisite does NOT work here. Alpha Mechs
             declares it once on four Abstract parents
             (AM_LightMechanoidRecipe, AM_MediumMechanoidRecipe,
             AM_HeavyMechanoidRecipe, AM_SuperHeavyMechanoidRecipe) and the 26
             concrete recipes inherit it. PatchOperations run on the raw XML
             BEFORE ParentName inheritance is resolved, so a predicate on
             researchPrerequisite sees only the four abstracts, and deleting
             those would leave 26 children pointing at a missing parent.

             Match the children by ParentName, then the parents by Name. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationRemove">
          <xpath>/Defs/RecipeDef[starts-with(@ParentName,"AM_") and contains(@ParentName,"MechanoidRecipe")]</xpath>
          <success>Always</success>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationRemove">
          <xpath>/Defs/RecipeDef[starts-with(@Name,"AM_") and contains(@Name,"MechanoidRecipe")]</xpath>
          <success>Always</success>
        </li>
        <!-- Belt and braces for any AM recipe that does declare it directly. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationRemove">
          <xpath>/Defs/RecipeDef[starts-with(researchPrerequisite,"AM_")]</xpath>
          <success>Always</success>
        </li>

        <!-- 2. No crafting the mechanitor apparel. The recipeMaker goes,
                the ThingDef stays, so nothing that references the item by
                name breaks. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationRemove">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[starts-with(recipeMaker/researchPrerequisite,"AM_")]/recipeMaker</xpath>
          <success>Always</success>
        </li>

        <!-- 3. No buying it either. Every AM_ item loses its tradeTags, so
                no stock generator can offer one. Also covers the prestige
                gear that the Royalty and VFE Pirates submodule patches add,
                which have no recipeMaker of their own. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationRemove">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[starts-with(defName,"AM_")]/tradeTags</xpath>
          <success>Always</success>
        </li>

        <!-- 4. No building the band nodes, boosters and rechargers.
                Dropping designationCategory takes them out of the architect
                menu entirely, and unlike deleting the def it cannot dangle. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationRemove">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[starts-with(researchPrerequisites/li,"AM_")]/designationCategory</xpath>
          <success>Always</success>
        </li>

        <!-- 5. Finally, out of the research tree. Safe now that nothing
                above depends on these to stay locked. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationRemove">
          <xpath>/Defs/ResearchProjectDef[starts-with(defName,"AM_")]</xpath>
          <success>Always</success>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
